{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917237114},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a calculation about farmers markets per 100,000 residents. They've provided two data sources:\n1. US farmers markets by state dataset\n2. Census data with population information\n\nFollowing the xorq analyst instructions, I should:\n1. First check if there are semantic models in the catalog\n2. List declared aliases\n3. Only ingest if no existing alias covers the data\n4. Use xorq_select to obtain values\n5. Compose any derived metrics into the catalog\n6. Verify all numbers using xorq_verify\n\nLet me start by orienting to the catalog and checking what's available.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking what's available in the catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Cz3sxL59qJ4Mv8YRoDXVfc","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014j81ZmE2ghHQ1sEPhjJv4D","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":288,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8302,"totalTokens":8600,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.00144,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.0103775,"total":0.0118275},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":143},"stopReason":"toolUse","t